---
import AuthButton from '#membership/components/AuthButton.astro';
import '../styles/global.css';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
    <meta name="description" content="A local Astro app that exercises the membership integration." />
    <title>astro-discord-membership playground</title>
  </head>
  <body>
    <main class="playground">
      <p class="eyebrow">Integration fixture</p>
      <h1>astro-discord-membership playground</h1>
      <p class="intro">
      This minimal host app loads the local integration through <code>file:..</code> and exposes its Discord sign-in flow.
      </p>

      <div class="actions">
        <AuthButton />
        <a href="/members">Open member directory →</a>
      </div>

      <div class="notice">
        <strong>Before testing protected routes</strong>
        <p>
          Copy <code>.env.example</code> to <code>.env</code> and provide Discord, Firebase, session, and SMTP credentials.
          The home page itself does not require credentials; the directory and profile routes do.
        </p>
      </div>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
